<title>USA: Calif. Health $37 mln repriced, restructured.</title>
<headline>Calif. Health $37 mln repriced, restructured.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber Inc. said it repriced and restructured a $37.16 million California Health Facilities Financing Authority insured health facilities refunding revenue bond issue for Valley Care Hospital Corporation, Series 1997, cutting the yield in 2020 to 5.737 percent from 5.75 percent and raising the size of the issue to $37.16 million from $37.11 million.</p>
<p>RE: $37,165,000</p>
<p>CALIFORNIA HEALTH FACILITIES FINANCING AUTHORITY</p>
<p>INSURED HEALTH FACILITIES REFUNDING REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>(VALLEY CARE HOSPITAL CORPORATION)</p>
<p>SERIES 1997</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE REPRICING OF THE 2020 MATURITY.</p>
<p>WE HAVE RECEIVED THE VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: NR		    S&amp;P: A+</p>
<p>						CAL MTGE INS</p>
